Hibernation theory
It was believed that birds hibernated underwater or buried themselves in ___
This theory was later disproved by experiments on caged birds.

Transmutation theory
Aristotle believed birds changed from one species into another in summer and winter.
In autumn he observed that redstarts experience the loss of ___ and thought they then turned into robins.
Aristotle's assumptions were logical because the two species of birds had a similar ___

17th century
